Z||000000||fieroman_5000||10-20-2001||09:46 PM||||Really...I have an '84 SE 4 banger automatic. I don't get nearly as much HP as I would like. I'm thinking of putting a 6 'er in it. I know ,I know it's harder that any other years and models. but it can't be that bad...can it?<P>And what are the prices approximately?<BR>I don't need a New one.<P>Fieroman||||reg||12
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-20-2001||09:51 PM||||someone will be along that knows for sure, but I think theres some wiring issues since 84 didnt have a V6 avail. If you want more go, when you do the swap, Id go with a stick. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-20-2001||09:56 PM||||You have to completely re-wire the entire car......a huge PITA.  You would be better off getting one with a V-6 already installed or at least getting an '85-'88 4-cyl. to start with......these don't need to be re-wired completely.<P>'85 V-6 SE's are fairly common and pretty cheap to find......I would just go that route myself.....save yourself some aggravation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||10-20-2001||11:47 PM||||Try this thread and talk to the source.  He's been at this one for a while.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011131.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011131.html</A> <BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||dennis_6||10-21-2001||12:10 AM||||I don't understand why you would have to rewire the entire car.  If you splice the 4cyl harness with the v6 harness and recalibrate the tach what is the big deal?  If you can put a caddy v8 in 84 without much trouble why is it so hard to put a 6 in?  The only difference is the motor.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||10-21-2001||12:26 AM||||     It would be great for you to be able to get the V6 horsepower, but I tend to agree that getting an 85GT or SE would be a good place to start. My first Fiero was an 86SEV6 and I liked that car even more than my 88GT.<BR>     I'm sure that you could either hold on to your 84 to run you around for parts for your new addition, or sell it to get you at least half the money for your new car. I have no idea what they go for in your area.<BR>Whatever you decide to do, the best of luck. I'll be watching this topic.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||10-21-2001||08:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroman_5000:<BR><B>Really...I have an '84 SE 4 banger automatic. I don't get nearly as much HP as I would like. I'm thinking of putting a 6 'er in it. I know ,I know it's harder that any other years and models. but it can't be that bad...can it?<P>And what are the prices approximately?<BR>I don't need a New one.<P>Fieroman</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Fieroman!<BR>Prices will depend on what you pay...<BR>Example, I bought an Olds with a series I 3800 running for $100.00...<BR>Now I have the engine, computer, and wiring harness I need to do the swap...<BR>I am going to spend about $1500 in rebuilding and hopping up the engine, then who knows in installing it...<BR>I am doing all the work myself, so say $500 to install and wire...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
